<speak>
<s>This is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">04072026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>In the Rohingya camps of Bangladesh, child marriage rose twenty-one percent last year after United States aid cuts shuttered the schools that kept girls in class.</s> <s>Teachers describe the mechanism plainly... a budget line erased in a distant capital, and a girl handed into marriage within weeks.</s> <s>One of them, Maryam, was thirteen when her school closed — she's now fourteen, pregnant, and barred by her in-laws from ever returning to learn.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Russia fired ballistic missiles, cruise missiles and drones across five districts of the Kyiv region overnight, killing two people and wounding eleven in the first strike on Ukraine's capital in two weeks.</s> <s>Rescuers are still digging through a collapsed nine-storey building, and Poland scrambled fighter jets to guard its own airspace as the barrage unfolded.</s> <s>After more than three years of war, the pattern holds — a lull, then a return to the capital, each time testing how much Kyiv's air defences can still absorb.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Sudan's South Kordofan, Rapid Support Forces drones have killed at least one hundred civilians since February, and in the town of Delling seven missiles killed two children and wounded their mother.</s> <s>The strikes knocked out El-Obeid's power plant, silencing the water pumps that a city besieged for eighteen months depends on, with no solar backup to fall back on.</s> <s>The <sub alias="U N">UN</sub> Security Council demanded a halt in June, yet the envoy tasked with enforcing it concedes the strikes have not stopped.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Yemen's Houthis have threatened to strike Saudi airports and vital assets, accusing Riyadh of sending warplanes to block an Iranian jet carrying more than two hundred wounded Yemenis home.</s> <s>The warning tests a truce brokered by the United Nations back in twenty twenty-two, a fragile calm that has otherwise held for years.</s> <s>Whether it survives may depend on whether either side wants to reopen a border war the wider world stopped watching.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Thousands of Albanians are now chanting for Prime Minister Edi Rama's resignation, in protests that began over a United States-backed resort planned for a protected flamingo wetland at Narta Lagoon.</s> <s>What started as a narrow environmental grievance has widened into anger over jobs, schools and the cost of living in this <sub alias="E U">EU</sub>-aspirant Balkan state.</s> <s>Rama has said nothing about whether he'll step down or call fresh elections.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Analysts warn that Indonesia's government is sidelining its own academics, think tanks and technical bodies from the work of making policy.</s> <s>In the world's largest Muslim-majority democracy, they argue, backsliding shows up first not as the suspension of elections but as the quiet erosion of expertise.</s> <s>Commentators want the technical institutions restored before failures compound across health, the economy and disaster response.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Washington has banned China's fishing fleet from Pacific waters, hoping to outcompete Beijing in a contested ocean.</s> <s>Yet those waters are the most valuable shared resource the island states of the Blue Pacific guard, and a unilateral move on them reads to many like the old extractive playbook.</s> <s>Pacific governments have not said whether they'll back the American approach — and their trust, once spent, is hard to rebuild.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Syria's new People's Assembly seats two hundred and ten members, and no single bloc holds a majority.</s> <s>Its elected members rose not through parties but through wartime networks — Sharia councils, field hospitals, armed factions — with al-Sharaa appointing seventy more himself.</s> <s>Whether those networks harden into real parties or stay closed circles of loyalty is the question that will shape the country's next chapter.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>India brought a refinery worth seventy-nine thousand crore rupees online this weekend at Pachpadra, in the desert of Rajasthan.</s> <s>The plant turns nine million tonnes of crude a year into fuel and petrochemicals, and it opened the same day as a chip plant in Gujarat aiming for five billion semiconductors annually.</s> <s>The strategy beneath the ribbon-cutting is sovereign capacity — India means to process and manufacture at home rather than export raw crude and import the finished goods.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Nigeria's top court has freed the crude cargo aboard the seized vessel Tamara Tokoni, ruling that a loan dispute was contractual, not a matter for admiralty jurisdiction.</s> <s>A five-judge panel found the lower courts had no authority to hold the ship at all.</s> <s>General Hydrocarbons still owes First Bank one hundred and twelve thousand dollars from an earlier award, so the fight over the oil is far from settled.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A decade of survey data from Italy shows that it's anxiety about future finances, not present income, that predicts who stops visiting museums and reading books.</s> <s>The fear of what might go wrong, more than poverty itself, quietly shrinks a person's cultural life.</s> <s>The effect falls hardest on less-educated and childless adults, hinting at how a cost-of-living crisis hollows out civic and cultural participation.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>A single substation fault at Havana's Victoria de Giron plant blacked out the whole of Cuba, tripping two power units nationwide.</s> <s>The island's grid leans on aging, fuel-starved stations, so one broken part cascades into darkness for an entire country.</s> <s>Cuba's energy company hasn't said when full power will return.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Across two hundred and eighty-two Chinese cities, researchers found that wider gaps in education track with higher carbon emissions per person.</s> <s>The link runs through innovation — unequal schooling slows the spread of green technology and the upgrading of industry.</s> <s>The manuscript is an early, unedited release still awaiting peer review, so treat it as preliminary for now.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In carpenter ant colonies, scientists have found that a wounded nestmate isn't treated by the most experienced nurse, but by transitional workers switching between roles.</s> <s>Who tends the injured turns out to be a matter of where an ant sits in the colony's network, not how skilled it is.</s> <s>The finding reframes the division of labour itself as a problem of position rather than expertise.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>As Australia marks fifty years of NAIDOC Week, researchers warn that artificial intelligence could become the next extractive technology — ingesting Indigenous knowledge without consent, credit or return.</s> <s>They argue that the provenance of training data is a design choice, and that data sovereignty must be built into model pipelines rather than bolted on late.</s> <s>Nothing about us, without us... translated into the concrete questions of licensing, consent and who benefits.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Homes in Switzerland can now get twenty-five gigabit fibre, while many households in the United States are still offered just one.</s> <s>The Swiss treat fibre as a natural monopoly, mandating open access so rival providers share a single line, rather than letting one firm own both the network and the service.</s> <s>The gap, one analyst argues, will persist until regulators decide the wire beneath the street belongs to everyone who uses it.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>